{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CRITERION 1's SECOND CLAUSE IS NOW ACTUALLY CHECKED — the 86 Gerrit votes, not \"it rests on the gate\"\n\nThe independent AC-verification comment was explicit that it had NOT done this:\n\n> their 32 individual Gerrit votes were NOT re-checked, so that clause rests on the gate.\n\nResting on the gate is a reasonable prior — Gerrit's submit rule requires both labels — but it is an\ninference about a CONFIGURATION, not an observation of what happened, and it cannot see an admin\nsubmit or a rule change. Since ticking criterion 1 asserts the clause, I checked it directly against\nthe Gerrit REST label data for every merged change.\n\n**Method.** Fetched the 300 most recent `status:merged project:rebar` changes with `o=LABELS` +\n`o=CURRENT_COMMIT`, matched each commit message against this epic's 36 children (both the\n`rebar-ticket:` trailer's full id and the leading `<short>:` subject form), and asserted\n`labels.Verified.approved` AND `labels.LLM-Review.approved` on every match.\n\n**Result: 86 merged changes attributed to 30 of the 34 closed children, and EVERY ONE carries BOTH\n`Verified +1` AND `LLM-Review +1`. Zero exceptions, so no change reached `main` without both gates.**\n\n### The four closed children with no directly-matched change — each resolved, not waved through\n\n * **0059** — closed `--class duplicate`, `duplicates 23ed`. A duplicate ships no change of its own;\n   the clause is vacuous for it.\n * **5f48** — closed `--class plan_defect`, `discovered_from b4e3`. Its fix was FOLDED into b4e3's\n   change (commit `36e134401`, whose message records \"Folds in bug 5f48\"). That change is in the 86\n   and carries both votes. The scan missed it only because the fold is named in prose, not as a\n   second trailer.\n * **b586** — a PARENT story whose work landed through its own two children (`f2f3`, `6758`), which\n   are grandchildren of this epic and so outside a direct-children scan. Checked explicitly:\n   **1179** (f2f3, retry-cluster extraction), **1185** and **1190** (6758, Retry-After on 429) — all\n   MERGED with `Verified +1` and `LLM-Review +1`.\n * **d103** — fixed by change **1209** under 727f's trailer (\"one cause, two observables\"). Checked\n   explicitly: MERGED, `Verified +1`, `LLM-Review +1`.\n\nSo all 34 closed children are accounted for, and every landed change behind them passed both gates.\nThe remaining obstacle to criterion 1 is only that **39c1 and 5200 are still `in_progress`** — the\n\"every child story is closed\" half, not the vote half.\n\n**Scope limit, stated so the next reader does not over-read this.** The 300-change window covers the\nwhole epic comfortably (the oldest matched change is well inside it), but this checks the votes on\neach change's CURRENT state. It does not audit whether an earlier patchset was submitted and later\namended, which Gerrit's model does not permit anyway."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785782967988552001,"uuid":"37a1420c-cb07-4245-adcf-aae498bb019d"}